 for Logo_MAC (white bg 93x33): in header on white bg fine; in footer (dark), the logo frame white bg would show as white rect — must clear frame fill; the glyph vectors: 33x33 lime shape + 14x14 dark + 49x18 dark text — on dark footer, dark vectors invisible. Override fills to white for the two dark vectors in footer instance. Doable via traversal.\n\nSocial logos: components like Logo_Facebook 10x20 vector fill dark #1A1A1F. On footer, override to white.\n\nOK writing Script 1 now. I'll also load all fonts here.\n\nCode:\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getPageByIdAsync(\"4:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\n\nconst fonts = [[\"Plus Jakarta Sans\",\"Regular\"],[\"Plus Jakarta Sans\",\"Medium\"],[\"Plus Jakarta Sans\",\"SemiBold\"],[\"Plus Jakarta Sans\",\"Bold\"]];\nfor (const [family, style] of fonts) await figma.loadFontAsync({family, style});\n\n// clone reference components into workspace\nconst refIds = {\n  Button:\"1:28\", Logo_MAC:\"2:16\",\n  Logo_Facebook:\"2:13\", Logo_Instagram:\"2:14\", Logo_LinkedIn:\"2:15\", Logo_Twitter:\"2:17\",\n  Icon_Arrow_Left:\"2:2\", Icon_Arrow_Right:\"2:3\", Icon_Bell:\"2:4\", Icon_Chevron_Down:\"2:5\",\n  Icon_Mail:\"2:6\", Icon_Map_Pin:\"2:7\", Icon_Minus:\"2:8\", Icon_Phone:\"2:9\", Icon_Play:\"2:10\",\n  Icon_Plus:\"2:11\", Icon_Trending_Up:\"2:12\"\n};\nconst comps = {};\nconst info = [];\nlet x = -2400, y = 0;\nfor (const [name, id] of Object.entries(refIds)) {\n  const orig = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  const c = orig.clone();\n  c.name = \"MAC/\" + name;\n  page.appendChild(c);\n  c.x = x; c.y = y;\n  x += 260; if (x > -600) { x = -2400; y += 140; }\n  comps[name] = c;\n  // clear frame bg fill so instances are transparent\n  const paintInfo = {name};\n  if (\"fills\" in c) { paintInfo.frameFills = JSON.stringify(c.fills); c.fills = []; }\n  // find vectors\n  const kids = [];\n  const walk = (n, d) => { for (const ch of (\"children\" in n ? n.children : [])) {\n    kids.push({t: ch.type, n: ch.name, w: Math.round(ch.width), h: Math.round(ch.height),\n      fills: \"fills\" in ch ? JSON.stringify(ch.fills).slice(0,120) : null,\n      strokes: \"strokes\" in ch ? JSON.stringify(ch.strokes).slice(0,120) : null, d});\n    walk(ch, d+1);\n  }};\n  walk(c, 0);\n  paintInfo.children = kids;\n  info.push(paintInfo);\n}\nfigma.currentPage = page; // not needed\nreturn JSON.stringify({ids: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(comps).map(([k,v])=>[k,v.id])), info}, null, 1);\n```\n\nHmm wait: cloning COMPONENT nodes — clone of a component is a component. Good. But careful: clearing fills on the cloned component frame — Logo glyph visibility: Logo_MAC's white bg removed is fine.\n\nBut icons: frame fill white — after clearing, vector visible. Good.\n\nReturn ids map for later scripts.\n\nLet me also double check `figma.getPageByIdAsync` exists — yes (getPageByIdAsync in newer API). And setCurrentPageAsync(page).\n\nNow write Script 1.","signature":"62babb684d52457889ad7ebc"}],"id":"974337d3-c845-4b8e-8775-84af82a544a8","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec9f4e39-381d-40ad-99ab-9aedc1b573bb","uuid":"c02d12a8-1927-462f-a0d5-79ba5b70ddf5","timestamp":"2026-11-02T00:53:58.575Z","thinking_duration_ms":173801}
