go instance (93x33) | nav row (H gap 28): 5 NavItems | right: bell IconButton + Btn_Dark \"Get started\". \n\n16. **MAC/Footer**: 1440x~420 dark #010205 pad 80/64: top row: left col w 480: logo + desc 14 onDark lh 24 + social row (4 icons 24 white) | spacer | columns: Navigation (title 14 SemiBold white? Column titles \"Navigation/Licence/Contact\" — data gives them), links 14 onDark lh 36? Contact rows with icons lime.\n   Bottom: divider rgba white 12% + ? no extra copy. Maybe row: logo small + \"©\" no — Copyright is listed under Licence column as a link \"Copyright\". OK no bottom bar. Actually add divider + social? Social icons: under logo desc. Fine.\n\nLayout for footer: 4 columns: brand (480) + Navigation + Licence + Contact. Column gap 64. Navigation/Licence titles 14 SemiBold ink→white, links 14 Regular onDark, gap 12. Contact rows: icon 20 lime + text 14 onDark, gap 12 vertical.\n\nHeader height 88: nav text 16.\n\n**Page sections** (in 01_Home, auto layout vertical width 1440):\n1. Header instance\n2. Hero section: pad 80 top 64 bottom 88; H layout gap 64: left col w 620: H1 (54, wrap), sub 18 text2 mt 24 (FILL w), buttons row mt 40 gap 16: Btn_LimeIcon \"Schedule Call\" + Btn_Outline \"View Case Study\". right col w 560: vertical gap 24: StatCard (560 w), ChartCard (560 w).\n   Hmm hero right column heights: statcard ~ 250 + chart ~ 240 = 514; left H1 3 lines 198 + sub 56 + buttons 56 + gaps = ~370. OK.\n3. Trusted: pad 80, h ~150: center column gap 28: label \"Trusted by the world's biggest brands\" 14 text3; row gap 72: wordmarks \"Paywise\" \"Campfield\" \"Mazeline\" 26 Bold ls 1 ink opacity 0.85. Maybe bg surfaceAlt full-bleed? Keep white with top border? I'll give section bg white; add hairline top/bottom border? Keep clean.\n4. About: bg surfaceAlt (#F6F7F2), pad 96 80: row gap 64: left H2 \"Provide the best service with out-of-the-box ideas\" (40, w 560, 3 lines); right col w 600: paragraph 18 lh 30 text2 + maybe stat mini row? Only given copy. Add lime accent bar above paragraph? A 48x6 lime bar — decorative, fine. Paragraph + maybe second block: none. It'll look sparse; add big quote mark? Keep bar + paragraph. Also could add small badge row: \"SEO\" chips — invented copy, skip.\n5. Case studies: bg ink, pad 96 80: heading \"Real-world examples...\" white 40 w 720; filters row mt 32 gap 12 (4 tags, second selected); cards row mt 48 gap 24: CaseCardHover (410), CaseCard (Ai Corporation), CaseCard (Lancer).\n   CaseCard instance text overrides: caption + title.\n6. Projects & video: white, pad 96 80: row gap 64: left w 420: \"920+\" 64 Bold; \"Projects finished superbly\" 18 text2 mt 12; avatars row mt 40: 4 Avatar instances overlapped (-12 margin? overlap in auto layout needs negative spacing — itemSpacing can't be negative per-item; use itemSpacing -12 on the row? Auto layout supports negative itemSpacing? Yes, itemSpacing can be negative in Figma auto layout). Set row itemSpacing -12, then \"+\" chip: 48 circle lime with Icon_Plus ink 20 + ml extra. right: VideoBlock 720x440.\n7. Testimonial: bg surfaceAlt pad 96: center column w 880: quote 26 Medium lh 40; mt 40 row: avatar 64, name/role stack; mt 40 pager row: \"01/05\" + arrow buttons. Center everything.\n8. Blog: white pad 96 80: header row: H2 w 680 left; right: \"See more\" link (14 SemiBold + arrow icon) aligned bottom. paragraph 16 text2 mt 16 w 680. cards row mt 48 gap 24: 3 ArticleCards.\n9. FAQ: bg surfaceAlt pad 96 80: row gap 64: left w 480: H2 \"Digital Marketing FAQs\"; para 16 text2 mt 16; buttons row mt 32: Btn_Outline \"More Questions\" + Btn_Dark \"Contact Us\". right w 656: FAQ items: expanded instance + 3 collapsed.\n10. CTA: white pad 0 80 96: CTABanner 1280.\n11. Footer instance.\n\nThen 01_Home frame: auto layout vertical, w 1440 hug h, bg white, name \"01_Home\", x 0 y 0 (or 100). Components sheet at x -3000.\n\nTotal build = several scripts. Let me be careful with auto layout API:\n- f.layoutMode = \"VERTICAL\"/\"HORIZONTAL\"\n- f.primaryAxisSizingMode = \"AUTO\"/\"FIXED\"; f.counterAxisSizingMode = \"AUTO\"/\"FIXED\"\n- f.paddingLeft/Right/Top/Bottom; f.itemSpacing\n- f.primaryAxisAlignItems = \"MIN\"|\"CENTER\"|\"MAX\"|\"SPACE_BETWEEN\"\n- f.counterAxisAlignItems = \"MIN\"|\"CENTER\"|\"MAX\"|\"BASELINE\"\n- f.layoutSizingHorizontal = \"FILL\"|\"HUG\"|\"FIXED\" (on children within auto-layout parent)\n- f.resize(w,h) for fixed.\n\nFor text inside auto layout: t.layoutSizingHorizontal=\"FILL\" then textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\" automatically? Setting FILL makes width fill; text height hug — need t.textAutoResize = \"HEIGHT\". Default textAutoResize is \"WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT\"; set to \"HEIGHT\" then FILL.\n\nRadius: f.cornerRadius = n; individual corners f.topLeftRadius etc.\n\nEffects: f.effects = [{type:\"DROP_SHADOW\", color:{r,g,b,a}, offset:{x,y}, radius, spread, visible:true, blendMode:\"NORMAL\"}].\n\nStrokes: f.strokes=[S(\"#E9EAEE\")]; f.strokeWeight=1; strokeAlign \"INSIDE\".\n\nComponent creation: const comp = figma.createComponent(); comp.layoutMode etc; then figma.createComponentFromNode(frame)? Easier: build a FRAME fully, then `figma.createComponentFromNode(frame)` converts. That preserves auto layout. I'll do that.\n\nInstance overrides: for text: inst.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\").characters = \"...\". Needs font loaded. For icons: instance.findAll(n=>n.type===\"VECTOR\").forEach(v=>{if(v.strokes.length)v.strokes=[S(hex)];else v.fills=[S(hex)];}) — on an instance of a component, setting fills/strokes on sublayers creates overrides — allowed.\n\nRescale icons: iconInst.rescale(16/24) — rescale changes width & height proportionally. For NavItem: chevron 16.\n\nText override caution: cloned default Button (6:2) text \"Button\" — override per instance.\n\nFor components where I need icon inside built via createInstance of MAC/Icon_X — fine.\n\nAlso: componets at negative x on page 4:2 — that's allowed (\"New frames, reusable components and prototype connections are allowed in this workspace\").\n\nOne risk: `figma.createComponentFromNode` exists. Yes.\n\nLet me now write Script 2: base primitives + buttons + nav + icon button + avatar + filter tags. I'll define shared helpers each time.\n\nAlso set page 4:2 backgrounds? Not needed.\n\nLet me carefully write Script 2 code:\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"4:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nfor (const s of [\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"]) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Plus Jakarta Sans\",style:s});\n\nconst comps = {\n  Button:\"6:2\", Logo_MAC:\"6:4\", Logo_Facebook:\"6:8\", Logo_Instagram:\"6:10\", Logo_LinkedIn:\"6:14\", Logo_Twitter:\"6:16\",\n  IcoArrowL:\"6:18\", IcoArrowR:\"6:20\", IcoBell:\"6:22\", IcoChev:\"6:25\", IcoMail:\"6:27\", IcoPin:\"6:30\",\n  IcoMinus:\"6:32\", IcoPhone:\"6:34\", IcoPlay:\"6:36\", IcoPlus:\"6:38\", IcoTrend:\"6:40\"\n};\nconst R = {}; for (const k in comps) R[k] = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(comps[k]);\n\nfunction hex(h){const n=parseInt(h.slice(1),16);return{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255};}\nfunction S(h,o){const p={type:\"SOLID\",color:hex(h)};if(o!==undefined)p.opacity=o;return p;}\nconst C={lime:\"#99EA48\",limeDeep:\"#77C62E\",limeSoft:\"#EAF9CE\",ink:\"#010205\",t2:\"#5B5E68\",t3:\"#8B8E98\",border:\"#E9EAEE\",alt:\"#F6F7F2\",ph:\"#E4E6EB\",phD:\"#CDD0D7\",darkCard:\"#14161B\",onDark:\"#A7AAB4\",white:\"#FFFFFF\"};\n\nfunction frame(name,dir,props){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;if(dir){f.layoutMode=dir;f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";}\n  const p=props||{};if(p.w!==undefined){f.resize(p.w, f.height);} // careful\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nHmm, resize on auto layout frame with sizing AUTO gets overridden. Standard pattern: set sizing modes first: for fixed width: counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" then resize. For VERTICAL layout: primary axis = vertical (height), counter = horizontal (width). So width fixed → counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" + resize(w, h anything) then height AUTO.\n\nI'll write helper:\n\n```js\nfunction AL(name, dir, o) {\n  const f = figma.createFrame();\n  f.name = name;\n  f.layoutMode = dir;\n  f.primaryAxisSizingMode = o.p||\"AUTO\";\n  f.counterAxisSizingMode = o.c||\"AUTO\";\n  if (o.w!==undefined||o.h!==undefined) f.resize(o.w||100, o.h||100);\n  if (o.pad){f.paddingTop=o.pad[0];f.paddingRight=o.pad[1];f.paddingBottom=o.pad[2];f.paddingLeft=o.pad[3];}\n  if (o.gap!==undefined) f.itemSpacing=o.gap;\n  if (o.bg) f.fills=[S(o.bg,o.bgO)]; else f.fills=[];\n  if (o.r) f.cornerRadius=o.r;\n  if (o.main) f.primaryAxisAlignItems=o.main;\n  if (o.cross) f.counterAxisAlignItems=o.cross;\n  if (o.stroke){f.strokes=[S(o.stroke,o.strokeO||1)];f.strokeWeight=o.sw||1;f.strokeAlign=\"INSIDE\";}\n  if (o.clip!==undefined) f.clipsContent=o.clip;\n  return f;\n}\nfunction T(parent, chars, size, style, color, o) {\n  o=o||{};\n  const t=figma.createText();\n  t.fontName={family:\"Plus Jakarta Sans\",style};\n  t.fontSize=size;\n  t.characters=chars;\n  t.fills=[S(color,o.o)];\n  if(o.lh) t.lineHeight={value:o.lh,unit:\"PIXELS\"};\n  if(o.ls!==undefined) t.letterSpacing={value:o.ls,unit:\"PERCENT\"};\n  parent.appendChild(t);\n  if(o.fill){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.layoutSizingHorizontal=\"FILL\";}\n  if(o.w){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.resize(o.w,t.height);}\n  return t;\n}\nfunction icon(name,color,size){const i=R[name].createInstance();i.rescale((size||24)/i.width);\n  i.findAll(n=>n.type===\"VECTOR\").forEach(v=>{if(v.strokes.length)v.strokes=[S(color)];else if(v.fills.length)v.fills=[S(color)];});\n  return i;}\n```\n\nWait: rescale on instance — method exists: node.rescale(scale). It's available on most nodes. Should be fine.\n\nNote icon() rescale: R[name].createInstance() gives 24x24 (frame). rescale(size/24).\n\nSocial logos have varying sizes; recolor + rescale to height 20-24.\n\nAvatar comp: \n\n```js\nconst av = AL(\"x\",\"VERTICAL\",{}); av.resize(48,48); av.cornerRadius=100; av.fills=[S(\"#E4E6EB\")]; av.clipsContent=true;\nconst head=figma.createEllipse(); head.resize(16,16); head.x=16; head.y=12; head.fills=[S(\"#BFC3CB\")]; head.constraints={horizontal:\"SCALE\",vertical:\"SCALE\"}; av.appendChild(head);\nconst body=figma.createEllipse(); body.resize(32,26); body.x=8; body.y=30; body.fills=[S(\"#BFC3CB\")]; body.constraints={horizontal:\"SCALE\",vertical:\"SCALE\"}; av.appendChild(body);\nconst cAvatar=figma.createComponentFromNode(av); cAvatar.name=\"MAC/Avatar\";\n```\n\nNote AL with no dir = plain frame; my AL requires dir — pass null and guard.\n\nButtons:\n\n```js\n// Lime + icon\nconst b1=AL(\"x\",\"HORIZONTAL\",{pad:[16,28],gap:10,bg:C.lime,r:100,cross:\"CENTER\",main:\"CENTER\"});\nT(b1,\"Schedule Call\",16,\"SemiBold\",C.ink);\nb1.appendChild(icon(\"IcoArrowR\",C.ink,20));\nconst cBtnLime=figma.createComponentFromNode(b1); cBtnLime.name=\"MAC/Button/Lime + Icon\";\n```\n\nHmm component naming with slash creates component set path naming — fine, name string arbitrary.\n\n```js\n// Outline\nconst b2=AL(...,{pad:[16,28],bg:null,stroke:C.ink? or border, r:100,cross:\"CENTER\"});\n```\nOutline button: border #010205 1.5? Use stroke ink 1.5, text ink. \"View Case Study\" / \"More Questions\".\n\nSmall white: pad [12,20], r100, white bg, text ink 14 SemiBold, maybe subtle shadow.\n\nBtn_Dark default clone: instance with text override:\n```js\nfunction darkBtn(label){const i=R.Button.createInstance();const t=i.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\");t.characters=label;return i;}\n```\nDefault Button is 232 wide FIXED? Component width 232 height 56 with auto layout? Original: COMPONENT 232x56, text at x89 (centered) — likely auto layout hug with padding 89? 232-54*? text 54 wide → padding (232-54)/2=89. If auto layout hug, changing text to \"Get started\" (longer) resizes hug. Need to check primaryAxisSizingMode of 6:2. I'll inspect in script: if it's fixed, set instance width hug? For instance of fixed-size component, I can set layoutSizing on ins