{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked me to complete a full product design in Figma file https://www.figma.com/design/2gQjVhLerEROFXf7hdo019/ (fileKey 2gQjVhLerEROFXf7hdo019). Explicit requirements:\n   - Read 「00·Start Here」 for the design task, reference 「01·Foundations」 for visual specs, reuse 「02·Components」 components, use 「04·Media」 assets, and deliver the complete design into 「03·Workspace」 (page 4:2, currently empty).\n   - Verify account via whoami: must be zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (confirmed).\n   - Preserve all reference pages and their nodes; do not replace them or create a different file.\n   - Per the brief in 00·Start Here: build exactly ONE frame named \"01_Home\" (desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode) for a digital marketing agency called \"MAC\". Single-page task — NO prototype connections needed (all buttons/links are entry only).\n   - Fixed: brand colors #99EA48 (lime) and #010205 (ink), typeface Plus Jakarta Sans for all UI text, all copy/data verbatim, media assets (logo, social logos, icons), and the default Button component must be reused.\n   - Mine to define: all other colors, type scale, spacing, radii, elevation, grid, layout, grouping, order, states (selected filter, card hover, expanded/collapsed FAQ).\n   - Must include on the frame: Header (Logo_MAC, nav Service/Agency/Case Study/Resources with chevrons + Contact, Icon_Bell, \"Get started\"), Hero (\"Stay ahead of the curve with our forward-thinking\" + sub + \"Schedule Call\" with Icon_Arrow_Right + \"View Case Study\"), Hero stats (\"230+\", caption, progress bar, Icon_Trending_Up badge, traffic card \"Drive More Traffic and Sales\"/\"Drive more traffic and product sales\" with 3-bar rising chart), Trusted by (\"Trusted by the world's biggest brands\" + Paywise/Campfield/Mazeline text wordmarks), About, Case studies (dark section, filters All Work[20]/UI/UX Design[10] selected/Digital Marketing[5]/Branding[5], 3 cards — first in hover state with \"See Details\", then \"Ai Corporation. 2023\"/\"Ai Wave - Ai Chatbot Mobile App\" and \"Lancer Corporation. 2023\"/\"App Lancer - Freelance Mobile App\"), Projects & video (\"920+\", \"Projects finished superbly\", 4 avatar placeholders + \"+\", video placeholder \"HOW WE WORK\" + Icon_Play), Testimonial (quote, Michael Kaizer, CEO of Campfield Corp, pager 01/05, prev/next), Blog (\"Digital Marketing & SEO Services That Grow Traffic & Increase Revenue\" + paragraph + \"See more\" + 3 article cards each \"5 min read\" with fixed titles/excerpts), FAQ (\"Digital Marketing FAQs\" + paragraph + \"More Questions\" + \"Contact Us\" + 4 questions with first expanded), CTA (\"Ready to work with us?\" + \"Get Started\" with Icon_Arrow_Right), Footer (logo + description, social logos Facebook/Twitter/LinkedIn/Instagram, Navigation/Licence/Contact columns with phone/mail/pin icons).\n   - Build reusable components; use image placeholders (no photography) for case thumbnails, video poster, avatars.\n   - Verify with screenshots of all screens; fix visible problems; finish with file URL, 03·Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, limitations.\n   - System prompt: include 'Reasoning summary:' before every tool call and in final answer; use only assigned file; unattended session (resolve choices via brief).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via MCP use_figma tool (50k char limit per call)\n   - `figma.getNodeByIdAsync` (NOT getPageByIdAsync — doesn't exist), `figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)`\n   - Font loading: `figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Plus Jakarta Sans\",style:\"Regular\"|\"Medium\"|\"SemiBold\"|\"Bold\"})` before any text creation (style is \"SemiBold\" not \"Semi Bold\" for this font)\n   - `figma.createComponentFromNode(frame)` to convert built frames into components\n   - Component cloning from reference pages: `orig.clone()`, rename with \"MAC/\" prefix, clear frame fills for transparency\n   - Instance overrides: text characters via `findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\").characters`, vector recolor via findAll + strokes/fills assignment, visible=false, layoutSizingHorizontal=\"FILL\"\n   - Icon recolor helper: vectors with strokes.length>0 get strokes override, else fills override\n   - `rescale(scale)` for resizing icon instances (e.g., 24→16/18/20px)\n   - Auto layout: layoutMode, primaryAxisSizingMode/counterAxisSizingMode (\"AUTO\"/\"FIXED\"), primaryAxisAlignItems (\"MIN\"/\"CENTER\"/\"MAX\"/\"SPACE_BETWEEN\"), counterAxisAlignItems, itemSpacing (negative allowed), layoutPositioning=\"ABSOLUTE\" for decor children\n   - Padding arrays must be 4 values [top,right,bottom,left] — 2-value arrays crash set_paddingBottom\n   - Constraints {horizontal:\"SCALE\",vertical:\"SCALE\"} enable avatar instance resize 48→64 with children scaling\n   - Design system: 80px side margins (1280 container), section stack order decided by me\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Figma page 0:1 (00·Start Here) — read; contains full brief + fixed data (all copy strings listed in section 1)\n   - Figma page 1:2 (01·Foundations) — read; brand colors/typeface confirmation\n   - Figma page 1:3 (02·Components) — read; default Button 1:28\n   - Figma page 1:4 (04·Media) — read; asset component IDs\n   - Figma page 4:2 (03·Workspace) — the build target; contains component sheet at negative x coordinates\n   - **Reference component IDs (cloned into workspace, originals untouched):** Button 6:2, Logo_MAC 6:4, Logo_Facebook 6:8, Logo_Instagram 6:10, Logo_LinkedIn 6:14, Logo_Twitter 6:16, Icon_Arrow_Left 6:18, Icon_Arrow_Right 6:20, Icon_Bell 6:22, Icon_Chevron_Down 6:25, Icon_Mail 6:27, Icon_Map_Pin 6: